            <ArticleTitle>Diagnosis and treatment of cuff tear arthropathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>33-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.JAA.0000469435.44701.ce</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rotator cuff tears account for a significant majority of shoulder pain presentations. Without diagnosis and management, advanced cuff tears may progress to cuff tear arthropathy, a degenerative arthritis condition of the shoulder. This article discusses the causes and management of cuff tear arthropathy, including definitive treatment with reverse shoulder arthroplasty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
